From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:19:17 +0200
Subject: Do not recheck the escaping uses of an export forwarder

An export forwarder passes its own parameters, and its type parameters
(bounded as the forwarded method bounds them), on to the method it forwards
to, which admits them. On 3.10, though, a type parameter bounded by a
capability class (`target <: Intake[medium]`, so `Intake^` in the bound)
counts as a use of the bound's root when passed on, which the escaping-uses
check reports as "Local any in the bound of type target leaks into capture
scope of method ingest": exporting such an extension method no longer
compiled (Soundness's `zephyrine.ingest`; 3.9 accepted it). Uses inside an
export forwarder are not checked again.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude Code).

Proscala-Patch: exportuses
